    "title": "DA: Former Oak Ridge officer indicted on 23 official misconduct charges - NewsBreak",
    "text": "Oak Ridge\nDA: Former Oak Ridge officer indicted on 23 official misconduct charges\n2 hours ago\nANDERSON COUNTY, Tenn. — A former Oak Ridge Police Department officer was indicted on \"official misconduct\" charges, according to the District Attorney General. A release from the DA said that an Anderson County Grand Jury returned indictments against Zachary Gauthier, 34, on 23 counts of official misconduct. The release said the matter came from complaints within the police department, with ORPD then contacting the DA for an independent investigation of the allegations.\n2",
